Package: uzunyx-lockkeys
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: plasma-workspace (>= 4:6.7), kwin-wayland (>= 4:6.7), qt6-svg-plugins, qml6-module-org-kde-plasma-workspace, qml6-module-org-kde-plasma-plasma5support, libkf6config-bin
Conflicts: waifbian-lockkeys
Replaces: waifbian-lockkeys
Description: Caps Lock and Num Lock indicator for the Plasma panel
 Plasma widget (org.uzunyx.lockkeys), an alarm for keyboards without lock
 key lights: a glossy pill, in the style of the Uzunyx window buttons, with an
 "A" half for Caps Lock and a "1" half for Num Lock. In the normal position
 (Caps Lock off, Num Lock on) a half is quiet, in the edition's accent colour;
 otherwise it fills with intense red and pulses, hard to miss.
 .
 Its option, "Caps Lock and Num Lock" (default) or "Caps Lock only" (for
 keyboards without a numeric keypad), also decides whether Num Lock is
 turned on at login. The system default, on, is set in /etc/xdg/kcminputrc.
